  "limitations": [
    "Both JS readers use OpenPGP.js 6.3.3 under Node in this native suite; they are independent of Go, not independent of each other. Actual Chromium coverage is separate.",
    "Throwaway secret packets are intentionally unprotected in private temporary directories; no owner key, attachment, passphrase or cloud archive is an input. Removal is not guaranteed secure erasure.",
    "The actual release-helper direction requires AES-256-OCB. This pinned high-level Go writer independently negotiates AES-256-GCM for fresh JS keys; signed preferences are not rewritten.",
    "Dependency/package checksums bind selected bytes, not security, publisher authenticity, reproducible builds or every RFC 9580/PQC algorithm.",
    "No GnuPG/PGPy v6, OpenKeychain/PGPony/Kleopatra GUI, physical-device, protected-v6-secret, owner decryption, new-recipient approval or encrypted APK delivery is inferred."
  ],
